# ar8030-transport-tx runtime configuration for the BetaFPV P1 SKY, sourced
# by /etc/init.d/S65ar8030-transport-tx. Overrides the package's default file
# (package/ar8030-transport-tx/files/etc/default/ar8030-transport-tx) -- see
# that file for the full set of variables.

# AR8030_TRANSPORT_TX_ENABLED=false

# -C pi: bitrate controller = link capacity feedforward + PI on the
# link-side queueing delay (ar8030-transport tx/bitrate_ctl.c), as on the
# Ascent; waybeam's ar9311 backend takes live video0.bitrate.
# -n 1000: lowest bitrate the controller asks for, = waybeam's floor on
# AR9311 (VENC_BITRATE_MIN_KBPS; 300 is CV610 only).
# Not the Ascent's -F/-D/-S: the ar9311 backend has no ROI (focus mode),
# no video0.fpsDivisor and no timing sidecar.
AR8030_TRANSPORT_TX_ARGS="-C pi -n 1000"

# AR8030 reset: GPIO23 (bank1 line0), active low. Only drivable through the
# artosyn_gpio driver (loaded from /etc/modules): its direction register is
# write-only, so /dev/mem pokes do not work (ml-kernel docs/artosyn-sdio.md).
# artosyn_gpio registers each bank as its own gpiochip at the vendor's fixed
# base (0, 23, 45, 71, 77, 83, 94), so global numbers match the vendor's.
AR8030_RESET_GPIO=23

# Bind button: GPIO42 (bank1 line19), active low (ml-kernel
# proxima-9311-air.dts). Startup power 200 mW (lifecycled: 22 dBm) instead of
# lifecycled's air default of 400 mW (26 dBm): the stock P1 configs top out
# at 22-23 dBm for its PA. Only applies while no power is persisted.
# --soc-temp-cmd/--overheat-c 105: as on the Ascent, at >= 105 degC SoC
# (/usr/bin/p1-temp, the protemp sensor) hooks.d/overheat stops waybeam,
# unloads the camera chain and shows a still "VTX OVERHEAT" frame
# (/usr/sbin/video-pause); hooks.d/resume brings the video back at
# --overheat-resume-c (default 95). 105 is also where the stock P1 goggles
# warn about the air temperature. Without airflow that only slows the P1
# down; /usr/sbin/heat-guard takes the AR8030 down too at 110.
# --standby-dbm 10: the stock Ascent's low-power mode against overheating on the
# ground -- 10 dBm while the FC is disarmed, configured power again on arm,
# and for the whole of an overheat pause, armed or not. msposd reports the
# FC's arm state (MSP_STATUS) through /usr/bin/armed.sh -> POST
# /api/v1/armed; lifecycled assumes armed until it does, so a P1 without an
# FC stays at full power.
# --link-policy 2: stock's runtime MCS policy for video_strategy 2, as on the
# Ascent -- same baseband firmware, same ground: uplink MCS table + range
# 1-2 and rfo_kikp; the goggles push the matching downlink table. See
# ar8030-transport common/ar8030_link_policy.h.
# --rf-path-b-off: one RF path, like the Ascent Lite -- port A fitted, port B
# unpopulated -- but the chip comes up with path B transmitting and
# receiving too. lifecycled switches it off the way stock does on the Lite
# (PRJ_CMD_RF_PATH_CTRL); tx_mode stays 2TX_STBC, as there (see
# artlynk-p1-vendor-firmware's make_ap_config()).
# Not --fem-ctrl: its FEM bit (>= 24 dBm) is the Lite's FEM wiring; the P1
# has a GSR5755. Only with an output-power measurement.
AR8030_LIFECYCLED_ARGS="--http-port 8899 --bind-gpio 42 --default-power 200 --soc-temp-cmd /usr/bin/p1-temp --overheat-c 105 --standby-dbm 10 --link-policy 2 --rf-path-b-off"
